  "question": "Does the exact source-emitted legacy nssd.org pdfurl still expose a PDF when only the first 4096 response bytes are read with a Range header?",
  "answer": "No. A single anonymous streaming GET with Range bytes=0-4095 returns HTTP 200 text/html, no Content-Range and no redirect. The first 4096 bytes are HTML for a domain-sale landing page whose title is www.nssd.org-官网首页 and which states the domain is for sale. The prefix does not begin with %PDF-. The connection is closed after 4096 bytes, so no full body is downloaded. The legacy pdfurl is therefore a dead historical field, not a current full-text route.",
